From 6748e3cad587020449af5a896f696f92be56fa98 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: EcoWoods Build <build@ecowoods.ca>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 19:51:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(process): main refuses commits, and an empty branch
 refuses to push (F-152)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

THE FAILURE

Seventeen illustrations, the manifest registration, a regenerated import table,
a clean build and 36 green guards were committed onto local `main` on
2026-08-27 and never reached production. Every command in the sequence behaved
exactly as documented. The composition was the defect.

  1. A recovery procedure was pasted as one multi-line block. Line two was
     `git checkout -b feat/provenance-art`.
  2. That branch already existed — an earlier attempt at the same procedure had
     created it before failing for an unrelated reason.
  3. `git checkout -b` on an existing branch exits 128 and LEAVES YOU WHERE YOU
     WERE. It does not switch, and it does not stop the rest of a pasted block.
  4. The next twenty commands ran on main. `git commit` printed `[main f1ed47d]`
     — the branch name is right there, and it reads as noise after a 300-line
     build log.
  5. `git push -u origin feat/provenance-art` pushed the stale branch pointer,
     which still equalled origin/main. Git reported "Total 0 (delta 0)" and
     "* [new branch]". A successful push of nothing looks exactly like a
     successful push.
  6. `gh pr create` finally said "head branch main is the same as base branch
     main" — the only honest error in the sequence, three commands too late.

Six steps, one real error message, twenty minutes before production disagreed.

WHY A HOOK AND NOT A BETTER PROCEDURE

Because the procedure was already correct and it still failed. Instructions that
depend on a human noticing one line of output inside a 300-line log are not a
control. The two places this could be interrupted mechanically are the commit
and the push, so both are now interrupted.

  scripts/hooks/pre-commit   NEW. Refuses a commit while main or master is
                             checked out. Step 4 now stops, and the seventeen
                             commands after it never run on the wrong branch.
                             Exempt: rebase, cherry-pick, revert, bisect, merge
                             and detached HEAD, all detected from .git state.
                             Escape: ECOWOODS_ALLOW_MAIN_COMMIT=1, or
                             --no-verify.

  scripts/hooks/pre-push     EXTENDED. Refuses to push a branch whose tip is
                             identical to origin/main. Step 5 now stops, and the
                             error names where to find the missing commits.

  scripts/verify-hooks.mjs   NEW, and first in `pnpm verify`. A git hook is the
                             easiest thing in a repository to lose — it lives
                             outside the working tree, it dies silently when
                             someone drops the executable bit, and nothing fails
                             when it stops running. This asserts both hooks
                             exist, are executable, carry a shebang, still
                             contain the logic that makes them worth having, and
                             that package.json still wires core.hooksPath.

                             Whether core.hooksPath is set in a given checkout is
                             reported loudly and never failed. CI clones have no
                             hooks and must not; a fresh clone would otherwise be
                             red before anyone could run the install.

It runs FIRST in the chain on purpose. `pnpm verify` is &&-chained, and a
process failure that can silence every later result should surface before the
results it would silence.

TESTED, NOT ASSUMED

Seven cases against real repositories: the F-152 sequence reproduced exactly
(`checkout -b` on an existing branch, exit 128, still on main); commit on main
refused; the documented recovery line safe when the branch already exists;
commit on a branch succeeds; ECOWOODS_ALLOW_MAIN_COMMIT=1 passes; rebase onto
main not blocked; empty-branch push refused and a branch with real work pushed
normally.

37 guards green.

